  "configuration_id": "config_020",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the goal is to establish a strong reference point in the most promising region of the design space. Config_020 combines the strongest available components: multimodal (both RNA and image), multiprofile (richer per-cell information), scgpt (a powerful pretrained generative RNA encoder), imagenet_vit_l (a large ViT image encoder), transformer aggregation (the most expressive pooling strategy for multiple profiles), and concat fusion (information-preserving, letting the classifier learn the optimal combination). Testing this 'all-strong' configuration first will (1) establish an upper-bound baseline, (2) confirm whether the multimodal + multiprofile paradigm is beneficial, and (3) provide a reference against which subsequent ablations (e.g., swapping to resnet50, avgpool, weighted fusion, or singleprofile) can be interpreted. Under a tight 10-experiment budget, anchoring the search with the most capable configuration maximizes the chance that the best-so-far accuracy is already competitive, while still leaving 9 experiments to explore and refine."
}

